1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Pause on a German line.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,000
Save the word, and it's on your phone
a second later.

3
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,500
You already watch more than an hour
of TV a day.

4
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,500
Lingo turns it into your German lesson.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Lingo sits on the Fire TV home screen.

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,000
One press, and today's clip
at your level is playing.

7
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,500
Two subtitle lines:
German, large and bright;

8
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:51,500
English, small and quiet.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,500
The marked word is the one
worth learning at your level.

10
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,000
Pause, and Lingo explains
the marked word:

11
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:09,000
what it means, and one grammar note.

12
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:16,000
At the end, a two-minute quiz
on your phone.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Tomorrow it asks again,

14
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:25,000
spaced further out each time
you get it right.

15
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,000
Your place in each clip is kept.

16
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:40,000
Amazon Transcribe writes the German line
with word timings,

17
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,500
and Amazon Translate the English one.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,500
Every line is cut
to subtitle reading limits.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,800
Amazon Nova Pro on Bedrock
writes the glosses,

20
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,500
and code builds the quiz from them.

21
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:59,800
Preparing a clip costs about 25 cents
in AWS calls,

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,800
so the same pipeline can run
on licensed catalogues.

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,300
Lingo Plus is a subscription through
Amazon's in-app purchasing,

24
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,000
shown here in sandbox.

25
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:12,400
Lingo shares vega-media-kit,
our open-source player

26
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,000
and subtitle library,
with our other entry, Described.

27
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:19,000
One UI package,
written for Fire OS and Vega;

28
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,200
Vega support is experimental.

29
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,000
The AWS stack is CDK,

30
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,500
and every rough edge we hit
is a friction log in the repo.

31
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:31,800
Lingo is for adults learning German
or English at home,

32
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,500
like the 363,466 people
who started an integration course

33
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,800
in Germany in 2024.

34
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:41,500
Next: more languages,
through Translate.
